TEXT -1296 -320 Left 6 ;This example shows a highloaded network with \n6 220kV lines and 6 110kV lines and 5 transformers\nThe voltage is held constant with two PV-elements\nThe slack is in node1 \nThe 220kV lines are 1x240mm2 and 20km length\nThe 110kV lines are 1x185mm2 and 5km length\nThe 115kV voltages are held high by means of \ntransformer tapings: (see l_=xx parameters of the trafos)\nThe loads/generators have no loadline shape (constant all over time)
TEXT -440 440 Left 5 ;For currents of cables execute\n.meas scripts\nActivate plot window and\nPress Menu: File/Execute .meas script
TEXT -152 1248 Left 2 ;For the active power lost of 220kV overhead lines plot\nV(p1)+V(p2)+V(p3)+V(p4)+V(p5)+V(p6)+V(p7)+V(p8)+V(p9)+V(p10)+V(p11)+V(p12)\nFor  the active power lost of 110kV overhead lines plot\nV(p20)+V(p21)+V(p22)+V(p23)+V(p24)+V(p25)+V(p26)+V(p27)+V(p28)+V(p29)+V(p30)+V(p31)+V(p32)+V(p33)\nFor the active power lost of transformers plot:\nV(p50)+V(p51)+V(p52)+V(p53)+V(p54)+V(p55)+V(p56)+V(p57)+V(p58)+V(p59)\n \nFor the reactive balance of 220kV overhead lines plot\nV(q1)+V(q2)+V(q3)+V(q4)+V(q5)+V(q6)+V(q7)+V(q8)+V(q9)+V(q10)+V(q11)+V(q12)\nFor the reactive balance of 110kV overhead lines plot\nV(q20)+V(q21)+V(q22)+V(q23)+V(q24)+V(q25)+V(q26)+V(q27)+V(q28)+V(q29)+V(q30)+V(q31)+V(q32)+V(q33)\nFor the reactive balance of transformers plot\nV(q50)+V(q51)+V(q52)+V(q53)+V(q54)+V(q55)+V(q56)+V(q57)+V(q58)+V(q59)
TEXT -8 -480 Left 6 ;Exercise1:\nChange  the load to equivalent loads with ctrl nodes\nAstablish a loadline with the loads_ctrl devices\nYou can also change also (timeline) the active power output \not the generators\n \n \nExercise2:: \nRegulate the 110kV voltage with transformer an c_batt at bus11\nTry to exchange the transformers with transformer with ctrl nodes \nand set the taping to hold the voltage between 110kV and 120kV
TEXT 800 1680 Left 5 ;Slack
